<title>INDIA: Indian interbank term money quotes - April 28.</title>
<headline>Indian interbank term money quotes - April 28.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are indicative</p>
<p>quotes (in percent) for interbank term money on April 28:</p>
<p>.</p>
<p> TERM		 Private	  State-run    Foreign</p>
<p>			banks	    banks	  banks</p>
<p> ---------------  ---------    -----------   ----------</p>
<p>    7  DAYS	 1.50/3.50     ---------    1.50-3.50</p>
<p>   14  DAYS	 3.50/4.50     ---------    2.00-4.00</p>
<p>   30  DAYS	 5.00/6.00     ---------    4.50-6.00</p>
<p>   60  DAYS	 7.00/8.00     ---------    6.00-7.50</p>
<p>   90  DAYS	 8.75/9.75     ---------    8.00-9.50</p>
<p>  120  DAYS	 9.25/10.25    ---------    ---------</p>
<p>  150  DAYS	 9.50/10.50    ---------    ---------</p>
<p>  180  DAYS	 9.50/10.50    ---------    ---------</p>
<p>    1 YEAR	 10.50/12.00   -----------   ---------</p>
<p>--</p>
<p>The indicative interbank term money quotes are based on contributions from the Centurion Bank, UTI Bank, Indusind Bank, Global Trust Bank, Andhra Bank, Bank of Nova Scotia, Citi Bank N.A., Deutsche Bank, Bank of America, ABN Amro Bank N.V., Standard Chartered Bank, American Express Bank, Bank of America,</p>
<p>HDFC Bank, Bank of India.</p>
<p>For more details contact Bombay money desk on (022) 265 9000</p>
